---
import Layout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About">
  <article class="detail">
    <p class="eyebrow">THE PROJECT</p>
    <h1>A collection you can inspect.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Languages, formats, and workflows—demonstrated, not just listed.
    </p>
    <section>
      <h2>What belongs here</h2>
      <p>
        Every language entry in one recorded GitHub Linguist revision has a
        catalog record. Appropriate examples print, render, store, query, or
        demonstrate a small native capability. The curated format collection has
        its own explicit targets.
      </p>
      <h2>What completeness means</h2>
      <p>
        The inventory can be comprehensive while the examples remain a work in
        progress. Missing examples, untested detection, and unavailable
        toolchains stay visible. We do not use Linguist overrides to inflate the
        language bar.
      </p>
      <h2>Built for learning</h2>
      <p>
        The repository is the collection; this site is a searchable view. The
        site never executes submitted code. Reviewed examples run locally or in
        isolated CI jobs, separated from publishing credentials.
      </p>
      <h2>Independent by design</h2>
      <p>
        GitHub Showcase is an independent community project, not an official
        GitHub product. Original code and examples use the MIT license. Upstream
        Linguist data retains its original attribution.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
